    "created_at": "2020-01-13T14:42:13Z",
    "updated_at": "2020-01-13T14:42:13Z",
    "body": "I notice that we currently have a test for `data:` at `html/cross-origin-embedder-policy/data.https.html` that Firefox passes whereby it inherits cross-origin embedder policy and enforces it, despite not being a secure context. The alternative is a network error for `data:` URLs, which I'm not sure is what we want?\r\n\r\ncc @whatwg/cross-origin-isolation ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
